{%- comment -%}
  About Us. Brief §13 called for it "singkat dan visual" — short and
  visual — and that shaped the first build of this section: one photograph,
  one paragraph. NEITHER SURVIVED, on instruction 2026-09-22: "foto nya
  gausah di page about" (drop the photo) and "copywriting nya masih kurang
  bgt, pls generate more" (the copy needs to say more). So this is now a
  text-only section with three short paragraphs instead of one, and the
  `image`/`asset` render call, its schema field, and the two-column layout
  that existed for it are gone entirely — not hidden behind a setting,
  removed, because the client's instruction was to not have a photo here at
  all rather than to leave one optional.

  THE FACTS ARE STILL ONLY THE ONES ON RECORD, EVEN THOUGH THERE IS MORE
  COPY NOW. "More copy" was read as "say more about what is already true",
  not "invent detail to fill space" — PRODUCT.md lists "About Us history,
  founder or team facts, production volumes" under things not to fabricate,
  and that rule didn't change just because the brief's "singkat" did. What's
  new in paragraphs two and three is not new facts, it's the brief's own
  design-direction adjectives (§14: modern, feminine, minimal, premium but
  approachable, timeless) applied to the ready-to-wear line, and the
  studio's documented responsiveness (PRODUCT.md's customer evidence: "Admin
  ramah", "responsif" — "the person answering is part of the product")
  applied to the closing line about custom apparel. Both are already-sourced
  facts about the brand, not invented ones.

  THE HEADING IS STILL THE BRIEF'S OWN LINE — §6's hero example, "Everyday
  Pieces, Made for You." — unchanged by this edit.

  THREE TEXTAREAS, NOT ONE BLOB WITH BLANK-LINE BREAKS. `snippets/copy`
  renders a `value` raw with no paragraph handling, and the theme's own
  precedent for a multi-line settings field (`size-guide`'s row list) pipes
  through `newline_to_br` for a table, not prose — three fields keeps each
  paragraph independently editable and placeholder-safe on its own, which a
  single field split on blank lines would not be.

  NO CTA, still. A "Shop now" button would put this page in competition with
  the hero and the two-ways doors that already carry that job.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-content flex-col gap-4 px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg">
  <div data-reveal class="wl-measure flex flex-col gap-4">
    <span class="text-micro uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-subtle">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.eyebrow, label: 'eyebrow', inline: true %}
    </span>

    <h1 class="text-h1 leading-h1">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading', lines: 2 %}
    </h1>
  </div>

  <div data-reveal class="wl-measure mt-4 flex flex-col gap-5">
    <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body_1, label: 'paragraph 1', lines: 3 %}
    </p>

    <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body_2, label: 'paragraph 2', lines: 3 %}
    </p>

    <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body_3, label: 'paragraph 3', lines: 3 %}
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "About story",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "No photograph, by instruction. Text only. Every paragraph should stick to facts already on record: brief §13's four (founding year, what Wear Label is, its focus, the custom-apparel side), brief §14's design-direction words, or PRODUCT.md's documented studio responsiveness. No founder, team or volume claim the studio has not itself supplied." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "About Wear Label" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Everyday Pieces, Made for You." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body_1", "label": "Paragraph 1", "default": "Wear Label is an Indonesian womenswear label, founded in 2020 around one simple idea: clothes should be comfortable enough for every day and versatile enough to wear again and again." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body_2", "label": "Paragraph 2", "default": "Our ready-to-wear collection (trousers, tops, cardigans and outerwear) is designed to be lived in, not just looked at. We keep the palette neutral, the cuts clean, and the details minimal, because a piece that's easy to style is a piece you'll actually reach for." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body_3", "label": "Paragraph 3", "default": "Alongside ready-to-wear, we also produce custom apparel: uniforms, merchandise and branded pieces for companies, schools, and organisations who want the same fit and finish for their own team. And whether you're ordering one piece or a hundred, you're talking to the studio directly: we answer our own messages, from Kota Bekasi." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "About story" }]
}
{% endschema %}
